Chronicle — diary + calendar PWA. Vanilla JS ES modules, HTML, CSS. Mobile-first.

Files:
index.html
js/: app.js, calendar.js, diary.js, events.js, gestures.js,
     holidays.js, ical.js, notifications.js, sync.js,
     themes.js, themeEditor.js, undo.js
css/: base.css, ribbon.css, week-view.css, day-card.css,
      expanded-day.css, modals.css, agenda.css, themes.css,
      responsive.css
assets/: icons.svg

Theme system:
data.settings stores uiTheme, uiThemeCustomVars, customUIThemes,
eventThemeOverrides, customEventThemes.
Always call applyUITheme() + injectEventThemeCSS() together.

Conventions:
ES modules, state in app.js, saveData() for persistence,
modals use history API, esc() for user content,
touch-first interactions, CSS variables everywhere.

Bug fixes + UI updates:
- Clear all data removes repeat occurrences
- Clear day deletes repeat occurrences
- Stabilise reminders
- Move undo/redo to top of main menu
- Remove Add Item (keep Add Event)
- Add recurring indicator in weekly view, expanded view, agenda
- Mobile settings menu: add vertical buffer + scrolling
- Replace settings menu with grouped collapsible layout:
  Appearance, Calendar, Data, Sync (chevrons, compact mobile spacing)
- Navigation: Left/Right = week; Up/Down = month; Up/Down jumps to first week of month
- Remove Google Photos, Attach Image, Mood Tag

Remaining Phase 2:
P2-GD Google Drive Backup
P2-7 Google Calendar Sync

Coding behaviour:
Use diff-only output.
No full file rewrites unless requested.
Keep answers short unless I ask for detail.

At session start, ask: “Which feature would you like to work on next?”


SMART CODE MODE (AUTO DEBUG ↔ DIFF):

You must decide the mode automatically based on my request.

──────────────────────────────
MODE SELECTION
──────────────────────────────

Use DEBUG MODE if:
- I include an error message
- I say “why”, “broken”, “not working”, “issue”, “error”
- Behaviour is unclear or inconsistent

Use DIFF MODE if:
- I ask to “fix”, “change”, “update”, “add”, “remove”
- I give clear instruction what to modify
- I reference a specific function or line to change

If unsure → use DEBUG MODE first.

──────────────────────────────
DEBUG MODE (ROOT-CAUSE FIRST)
──────────────────────────────

1. ROOT CAUSE
- Exact reason for the issue
- Reference specific lines / variables

2. WHAT IS BROKEN
- Actual behaviour that fails

3. WHY IT HAPPENS HERE
- Tie to this code (init order, DOM, scope, events, etc)

4. MINIMAL FIX OPTIONS
- 1–2 small targeted fixes only
- No rewrites, no restructuring

Rules:
- DO NOT output code changes yet
- DO NOT rewrite files
- DO NOT assume missing code — ask if needed

──────────────────────────────
DIFF MODE (SURGICAL PATCHES)
──────────────────────────────

- Output ONLY a minimal diff
- NEVER rewrite full files unless explicitly told
- NEVER refactor, rename, reorder, or restructure
- NEVER modify unrelated code

Context rules:
- Include file name
- Include function or nearest block
- Include 2–5 REAL lines above and below change
- NEVER invent missing context

Line numbers:
- Use them ONLY if I provided them
- Otherwise DO NOT fabricate them

STRICT FORMAT:

1. File path
2. Function/block name
3. Diff:

```diff
@@ location @@
  context
- old code
+ new code
  context
